(2)S
1200 11867 m
/Times-RomanR 549 ff
15  0 32 (     The second "altered" card involves two new provisions on  CARD 1.  First, the SALB parameter)W
1200 11543 m
15  0 32 (now provides access to spectral vectors \(wavelength, emissivity, and reflectivity\) from a selection of)W
1200 11219 m
15  0 32 (default options stored on a file called "refbkg'.  Negative values from -1 through -16 \(with  values of)W
1200 10895 m
15  0 32 (-7 through -12 available for user- specification\) will pick up any of an assortment of surface)W
1200 10571 m
15  0 32 (properties, including snow, forest, farm, desert, ocean, cloud deck and 4 sample grass models.  The)W
1200 10247 m
15  0 32 (size of these vectors is variable and the format is in ASCII.  \(Ref. Robertson, SSI\).)W
1200 9923 m
15  0 32 (     Second, the MDEF value on CARD 1 was previously limited to a value of 1, selecting the single)W
1200 9599 m
15  0 32 (set of prestored molecular  profiles for species for which MODEL \(1...6\) do not pertain \(O2, NO,)W
1200 9275 m
15  0 32 (SO2, NO2, NH3 and HNO3\) .  Now, when MDEF=2, the user will be allowed to specify the profiles)W
1200 8951 m
15  0 32 (for the new heavy molecules for which cross-sections have been specified.  These include nine)W
1200 8627 m
15  0 32 (chloro-fluorocarbons \(CFC's\), plus CLONO2, HNO4, CCL4, and N2O5, with the databases stored in)W
1200 8303 m
15  0 32 ('UFTAPX.asc'.  The specification of user-defined profiles is modeled after the MODEL=7 option in)W
1200 7979 m
15  0 32 (LOWTRAN, but only one set of units can be used for the whole set of heavy species.  The "default")W
1200 7655 m
15  0 32 (profiles for these heavy molecules are stored in BLOCK DATA XMLATM and are based on 1990)W
1200 7331 m
15  0 32 (photochemical predictions \(after M. Allen, JPL\).  Since some of the CFC's have increased by as much)W
1200 7007 m
15  0 32 (as 8%/year, the user might well wish to redefine these values.  Note that both CFC11 and CFC12 are)W
1200 6683 m
15  0 32 (now as much as 80% larger than the default profiles.)W
1200 6359 m
15  0 32 (     In general, for standard atmospheric models, six input cards are now required to run MODTRAN)W
1200 6035 m
15  0 32 (for a given problem. For any specific problem a combination of several of the fifteen additional)W
1200 5711 m
15  0 32 (optional control cards are possible. The formats for the six main cards, fifteen optional cards, and)W
1200 5387 m
15  0 32 (definitions of the input parameters are given below. Because of the similarity between the MODTRAN)W
1200 5063 m
15  0 32 (and LOWTRAN instructions, the changes will be highlighted and the numbering scheme will be)W
1200 4739 m
(altered.)S
